e\",\"description\":\"The attribute 'Audit Score: float between 0.0 and 100.0' quantifies the results of a security audit, expressed as a percentage from 0 to 100.\",\"min_value\":0.0,\"max_value\":100.0,\"enumeration_values\":null}],\"description\":\"The bind 'Perform Security Audit: Audit Score' specifies that the activity 'Perform Security Audit' requires the attribute 'Audit Score'.\"},{\"activity\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Bag Check\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Bag Check' activity includes inspecting customers' bags for potential security threats or stolen items.\"},\"attributes\":[{\"type\":\"integer\",\"name\":\"Customer ID\",\"description\":\"The attribute 'Customer ID: integer between 1 and 10000' is the unique identifier for each customer involved in bag checks or complaints.\",\"min_value\":1,\"max_value\":10000,\"enumeration_values\":null}],\"description\":\"The bind 'Conduct Bag Check: Customer ID' specifies that the activity 'Conduct Bag Check' requires the attribute 'Customer ID'.\"}],\"constraints\":[{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Monitor Store Entrance' must be the first activity to occur in the process.\",\"template\":\"Init\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Monitor Store Entrance\",\"description\":\"The 'Monitor Store Entrance' activity represents the continuous observation of the store's entrance to detect any suspicious behavior or unauthorized access.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Deactivate Alarm' must be the last activity to occur in the process.\",\"template\":\"End\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Deactivate Alarm\",\"description\":\"The 'Deactivate Alarm' activity involves turning off the alarm system after verification or resolution of the trigger.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity must occur at least once in the process.\",\"template\":\"Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity consists of documenting and reporting any security breaches or suspicious activities.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":1},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' must not occur in the process.\",\"template\":\"Absence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Emergency Drill\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' activity entails practicing emergency response procedures with the staff.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":1},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Exactly one of the activities 'Train Security Staff' or 'Conduct Emergency Drill' must occur in the process instance. This means that the process is compliant if only 'Train Security Staff' event occurs without any occurrence of 'Conduct Emergency Drill' event, or only 'Conduct Emergency Drill' occurs without any occurrence of 'Train Security Staff'. The process is non-compliant if both 'Train Security Staff' and 'Conduct Emergency Drill' occur, or if neither occurs. The constraint enforces a mutual exclusivity and a mandatory occurrence of one of the specified activities.\",\"template\":\"Exclusive Choice\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Train Security Staff\",\"description\":\"The 'Train Security Staff' activity consists of educating and preparing security personnel on new protocols and skills.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Emergency Drill\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Emergency Drill' activity entails practicing emergency response procedures with the staff.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If an 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity occurs, then a 'Review Security Footage' activity must eventually occur after the 'Inspect Security Cameras' event at some point in the same process instance. There is no requirement on how soon or what events may occur in between. Multiple 'Inspect Security Cameras' can be pending at the same time, and a single 'Review Security Footage' can fulfill the obligation for all preceding 'Inspect Security Cameras'. If 'Inspect Security Cameras' does not occur, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Review Security Footage'. This is subject to the activation condition A.Camera ID == T.Camera ID.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Security Cameras\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity involves checking the functionality and footage of security cameras to ensure proper surveillance.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Review Security Footage\",\"description\":\"The 'Review Security Footage' activity involves analyzing recorded video from security cameras to investigate incidents.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Camera ID == T.Camera ID\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Whenever an 'Alert Security Personnel' activity occurs, it must be immediately followed by an 'Escort Suspect' activity in the next event position, with no other events in between. This immediate succession ensures a direct and uninterrupted transition from 'Alert Security Personnel' to 'Escort Suspect'. Multiple 'Alert Security Personnel'-'Escort Suspect' pairs can exist in a process instance, each adhering to this immediate succession rule. Events of 'Escort Suspect' can occur elsewhere in the process but not between an 'Alert Security Personnel' and its corresponding 'Escort Suspect'. This is subject to the activation condition A.Security Level is High, the correlation condition A.Personnel ID == T.Personnel ID, and the time condition 0,5,m.\",\"template\":\"Chain Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Alert Security Personnel\",\"description\":\"The 'Alert Security Personnel' activity entails notifying security staff about a potential security issue or incident.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Escort Suspect\",\"description\":\"The 'Escort Suspect' activity involves safely guiding a suspected individual to a secure area or out of the premises.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Security Level is High\",\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Personnel ID == T.Personnel ID\",\"time_condition\":\"0,5,m\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"An 'Alert Security Personnel' event can occur only if it is immediately preceded by a 'Verify Alarm Trigger' event, with no other events occurring in between. There can be multiple 'Alert Security Personnel'-'Verify Alarm Trigger' pairs within the process, each adhering to this immediate precedence rule. 'Alert Security Personnel' may occur without being followed by a 'Verify Alarm Trigger', but 'Verify Alarm Trigger' cannot occur without such an immediate preceding 'Alert Security Personnel'. This is subject to the activation condition A.Alarm Status is Triggered and the time condition 0,10,m.\",\"template\":\"Chain Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Alert Security Personnel\",\"description\":\"The 'Alert Security Personnel' activity entails notifying security staff about a potential security issue or incident.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Verify Alarm Trigger\",\"description\":\"The 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity includes confirming whether an alarm activation is legitimate or a false positive.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Alarm Status is Triggered\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":\"0,10,m\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If 'Perform Security Audit' activity occurs in a process instance with an 'Audit Score < 50', then 'Update Security Protocols' must also occur in the same process instance, and vice versa. This mutual obligation ensures that neither event can occur without the other. The events can occur multiple times and in any order relative to each other. If neither event occurs, the constraint is still considered satisfied.\",\"template\":\"Co-Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Perform Security Audit\",\"description\":\"The 'Perform Security Audit' activity entails evaluating the overall security measures and identifying vulnerabilities.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Update Security Protocols\",\"description\":\"The 'Update Security Protocols' activity involves revising and improving the existing security procedures and guidelines.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Audit Score < 50\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Conduct Bag Check' activity must be followed by a 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity at some point later in the same process instance. Conversely, a 'Handle Customer Complaint' event can occur only if a 'Conduct Bag Check' event has occurred before it within the same process instance. This bidirectional and ordered dependency ensures that 'Conduct Bag Check' impose obligations for future 'Handle Customer Complaint', and 'Handle Customer Complaint' cannot occur without prior 'Conduct Bag Check'. Multiple 'Conduct Bag Check' and 'Handle Customer Complaint' are allowed, with each 'Conduct Bag Check' eventually leading to a 'Handle Customer Complaint' and each 'Handle Customer Complaint' being justified by a preceding 'Conduct Bag Check'. This is subject to the correlation condition A.Customer ID == T.Customer ID and the time condition 0,1,h.\",\"template\":\"Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Bag Check\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Bag Check' activity includes inspecting customers' bags for potential security threats or stolen items.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Handle Customer Complaint\",\"description\":\"The 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity involves addressing and resolving issues raised by customers regarding security or service.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Customer ID == T.Customer ID\",\"time_condition\":\"0,1,h\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' activity cannot be immediately followed by a 'Report Incident' activity; there must be at least one other event between them. Similarly, a 'Report Incident' event cannot be immediately preceded by a 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' event. This constraint allows multiple occurrences of 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' and 'Report Incident' in any order, provided they are not adjacent in the event sequence.\",\"template\":\"Not Chain Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Check Inventory Discrepancies\",\"description\":\"The 'Check Inventory Discrepancies' activity includes investigating mismatches between recorded and actual inventory levels.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity consists of documenting and reporting any security breaches or suspicious activities.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Report Incident' event is permitted to occur only if an 'Escort Suspect' event has occurred before it within the same process instance. 'Report Incident' that occur without any prior 'Escort Suspect' are violations of the constraint. Multiple 'Escort Suspect' can occur, and any number of events (including other 'Report Incident') can happen between an 'Escort Suspect' and a subsequent 'Report Incident'. This ensures that certain actions cannot proceed without the necessary prerequisites being met first. This is subject to the correlation condition A.Incident Type is Theft.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Report Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Incident' activity consists of documenting and reporting any security breaches or suspicious activities.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Escort Suspect\",\"description\":\"The 'Escort Suspect' activity involves safely guiding a suspected individual to a secure area or out of the premises.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Incident Type is Theft\",\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity cannot be preceded by a 'Deactivate Alarm' within the same process instance. If a 'Deactivate Alarm' event has occurred at any point before a 'Verify Alarm Trigger' event, then 'Verify Alarm Trigger' is disallowed. Multiple instances of 'Verify Alarm Trigger' and 'Deactivate Alarm' can occur, but all instances of 'Verify Alarm Trigger' must occur before any instance of 'Deactivate Alarm'.\",\"template\":\"Not Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Verify Alarm Trigger\",\"description\":\"The 'Verify Alarm Trigger' activity includes confirming whether an alarm activation is legitimate or a false positive.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Deactivate Alarm\",\"description\":\"The 'Deactivate Alarm' activity involves turning off the alarm system after verification or resolution of the trigger.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If a 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity occurs in a process instance with the condition that the 'Complaint Status is Resolved', then a 'Conduct Bag Check' activity must not occur anywhere in the same process instance. This means that the occurrence of 'Handle Customer Complaint' event prohibits any occurrence of 'Conduct Bag Check' event. However, if 'Handle Customer Complaint' does not occur, 'Conduct Bag Check' may occur freely. Multiple occurrences of 'Handle Customer Complaint' are allowed, provided 'Conduct Bag Check' does not occur at all in the process instance. This is subject to the activation condition A.Complaint Status is Resolved and the correlation condition A.Customer ID == T.Customer ID.\",\"template\":\"Not Responded Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Handle Customer Complaint\",\"description\":\"The 'Handle Customer Complaint' activity involves addressing and resolving issues raised by customers regarding security or service.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Conduct Bag Check\",\"description\":\"The 'Conduct Bag Check' activity includes inspecting customers' bags for potential security threats or stolen items.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Complaint Status is Resolved\",\"correlation_condition\":\"A.Customer ID == T.Customer ID\",\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Review Security Footage' activity and an 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity must not occur such that the 'Review Security Footage' event is followed by the 'Inspect Security Cameras' event at any point later in the same process instance. Similarly, an 'Inspect Security Cameras' event must not be preceded by a 'Review Security Footage' event. This means that once a 'Review Security Footage' occurs, 'Inspect Security Cameras' cannot occur afterward, and if an 'Inspect Security Cameras' event occurs, it cannot have been preceded by a 'Review Security Footage' event. Both events can occur in the same process instance, but not in the prohibited sequence.\",\"template\":\"Not Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Review Security Footage\",\"description\":\"The 'Review Security Footage' activity involves analyzing recorded video from security cameras to investigate incidents.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Security Cameras\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Security Cameras' activity involves checking the functionality and footage of security cameras to ensure proper surveillance.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null}]}"